-- FG circuit pilot S2s: port of Tools.ShippingChildTeleMainA onto the context-predicate bundles (RefLawsAOpsX / RefLawsATeleX); generated by a rename-only script (names + suffix X, `AdmCtx O.quiet` -> `O.adm`). No sorry/axiom/native_decide/TRUSTED/law.

/-! # The main endpoints with `T` replaced by its two remaining fields (unit T2)

`RefLawsATeleX.ofTeleLamX O htel hlam` builds the whole bundle from `O` and the two laws that are
still premises: `htel : ForallTelescopeLawAX O.quiet O.adm mref cref` (the `telescope` field's statement)
and `hlam : LamTelescopeLawAX O.quiet O.adm mref cref` (the `lamTelescope` field's statement). The two
`def`s (Tools/ShippingChildWalkA.lean) are the field types verbatim (checked here by using them as
the fields); `localDecl`/`letDecl` are `localDecl_of_OX` / `letDecl_of_OX` (PROVED from `O`).

What this achieves: `localDecl` and `letDecl` are PROVED (T1), and the laws the endpoints require
from OUTSIDE are reorganised from 4 items to 2.
  `T` versions : `O`, `hA`, `T : RefLawsATeleX` (4 fields), + the theorem's other premises
  `_tl` versions: `O`, `hA`, `htel`, `hlam` (2 fields)        + the same other premises
This is NOT a claim of logical strength: under `O`, the full `T` and the two remaining fields are
EQUIVALENT (`ofTeleLamX` builds `T` from them; projection gives them back from `T`). The `T`-taking
theorems are unchanged. `telescope`/`lamTelescope` remain an ADDED, UNPROVED boundary (their
workers are `opaque`); nothing here is a runtime-fit proof or a joint-satisfiability proof. -/

